30,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems catalogue-style projects have a better long-term legacy, while mechanism-focused ones often leave their central questions unresolved.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"We have a crisis in phenotyping technicians, but plenty of applicants for modelling and code posts.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"The animal facility is ready, but the glasshouses are completely booked. Also, the spectroscopy suite had a massive lapse in service.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Computing is currently free under the national agreement, but animal-unit costs have spiked. Shipping is also eating into the budgets.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Field sites are precarious due to fire and flooding, though the national repository is finally processing deposits quickly.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Ryuji, does the abundance of modelling staff make simulation-heavy projects a safer bet for delivery?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Precisely. The human capital is there for computation, whereas the biological technical support is vanishing.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Benjamin, if animal costs are rising and spectroscopy is unreliable, we should be wary of any project relying on those.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. The financial burden of vivarium work now falls more heavily on the awardee than it used to.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Midori,,"And we must avoid projects that rely heavily on field sites, given the recent environmental disruptions.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"It sounds as though we are leaning toward something stable, perhaps a data-driven or computational approach.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree. Avoiding live breeding colonies seems prudent, as they are prone to schedule overruns.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"I am concerned about any project requiring the glasshouses, as there is simply no room.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests that a project utilizing the free computing agreement would be the most economically efficient.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Midori,,I agree. A project that avoids the field and the glasshouse would be the least likely to be interrupted.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
