55,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"We have our candidates. A is Plant Drought, B is Amphibian Regeneration, C is Protein Folding, and D is the Microbiome Atlas.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate A needs glasshouses, and B needs animal facilities. Both face staffing or cost hurdles.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Victoria,,A is out due to glasshouse bookings. B is risky because of the animal costs Benjamin mentioned.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"C uses spectroscopy, which Victoria noted is unreliable, but it leverages the free computing agreement.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Midori,,"D involves field sites, which I found to be highly unstable. That makes it a risky choice.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"D is a catalogue-style project, which I noted often has the best long-term utility, despite the field risks.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,But the staffing for D's phenotyping would be a nightmare. C's modelling needs are easily met.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"If the spectroscopy suite is idle, C might struggle, but it is better than a fully booked glasshouse.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"C is the most financially viable. The computing is free, and it avoids the expensive animal rates.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Midori,,"I still worry about C's instrumentation, but D's field sites are a guaranteed disaster right now.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I can see the merit in C, though I prefer the legacy of D. However, stability is key.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I vote for C. The technical staff are available, and the risks are manageable.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Ryuji. C is the most feasible given the current facility constraints.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,C is the logical choice. It maximizes the grant's value by using centrally funded computing.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Midori,,I will support C. It avoids the environmental interruptions that would plague the others.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I will join you all. Let us hope the spectroscopy suite remains functional.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
